<title>SPAIN: Aznar says Spain met three EMU goals, deficit next.</title>
<headline>Aznar says Spain met three EMU goals, deficit next.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish Prime Minister Jose Maria Aznar said on Wednesday Spain had met three of the criteria for European economic and monetary union and was on the point of also reaching the deficit goal.</p>
<p>&quot;A year ago we had not completed any of the convergence criteria. Now we have met three on inflation, foreign exchange stability and interest rates,&quot; Aznar said in his speech in a debate on the state of the nation.</p>
<p>&quot;We are now also on the point of meeting the deficit criteria and in the coming months we will see the level of debt beginning to fall,&quot; he added.  </p>
<p>Aznar said as a result, Spain was in shape to participate in EMU.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2161</p>
</text>
